      0,
      'The Perceptual Quantizer, standardized as SMPTE ST 2084 in 2014, maps digital code values to absolute brightness levels according to a model of human contrast sensitivity across a much wider luminance range than traditional gamma curves. HDR10 and Dolby Vision content can specify highlights far brighter than SDR\'s roughly 100-nit reference while allocating enough code values to shadow detail. Hybrid Log-Gamma, developed jointly by the BBC and NHK, is a competing HDR transfer function designed to remain backward-compatible with SDR displays without separate metadata, more common in live broadcast HDR than cinema. Rec. 709 is the SDR broadcast standard, and S-Log3 is Sony\'s proprietary on-set log curve, not HDR standards.',
